Spec: Repository Bootstrap

Platform: Bash/Spec Kit 1.0.7/SpecDD CLI 1.1.1

Purpose:
  Reproduce the pinned development toolchain and activate a registrar-backed Spec Kit integration that materializes the local SpecDD bridge.

Owns:
  ./bootstrap.sh

References:
  ../integration/specdd/extension.sdd
  ../integration/specdd/workflow-overlay.sdd
  ../integration/specdd-preset/specdd-preset.sdd

Must:
  Bootstrap preserves the pinned Spec Kit, SpecDD CLI, and SpecDD framework versions.
  The active Spec Kit integration is `codex` so extension and preset commands can be registered under pinned Spec Kit `1.0.7`.
  Existing initialized repositories change active integration through supported Spec Kit integration commands.
  The local bridge extension and preset are installed from canonical repository source before verification.
  The structural SpecDD workflow overlay is installed through supported Spec Kit workflow-overlay commands.
  Check mode verifies bridge command materialization, preset augmentation materialization, lifecycle hook registration, workflow-overlay resolution, and `specdd lint` without changing repository state.

Must not:
  Patch generated Spec Kit commands, installed extension state, installed preset state, workflow-overlay state, or SpecDD framework files directly.

Done when:
  Bootstrap apply followed by check succeeds with the bridge and structural workflow gates available through the active Codex integration.
